<title>USA: Lumisys Inc Q3 net falls.</title>
<headline>Lumisys Inc Q3 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Income Statement (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>					   September 30,  September 30,</p>
<p>					  1996     1995    1996    1995</p>
<p> Sales			     $ 5,933  $ 5,013 $16,915$ 12,091</p>
<p> Cost of sales		     2,684    2,322   7,795   5,581</p>
<p> Gross margin			3,249    2,691   9,120   6,510</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>   Sales and marketing	     463	412   1,408   1,112</p>
<p>   Research and development    1,064	821   3,099   2,042</p>
<p>   General and administrative    621	540   1,828   1,322</p>
<p>Acquired in-process research</p>
<p>    and development		   --	 --	--   1,442</p>
<p>    Total operating expenses   2,148    1,773   6,335   5,918</p>
<p> Income from operations	  1,101	918   2,785     592</p>
<p> Interest income, net		238	 32     668     110</p>
<p> Income before income taxes    1,339	950   3,453     702</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for income</p>
<p>  taxes				  522     (47)   1,019   (724)</p>
<p> Net income			    817	997   2,434   1,426</p>
<p> Net income per share	     0.12     0.20    0.36    0.28</p>
<p>Shares used to compute net</p>
<p>  income per share		 6,805    5,096   6,829   5,104</p>
<p>Note - Q3 1996 net includes charge of $225,000.</p>
<p>Lumisys is now reporting earnings on a fully taxed basis. Using a tax rate of 39% for both 1996 and 1995 would have produced &quot;normalized&quot; third quarter net income of $817,000 and $580,000 respectively, an increase of 41%.  &quot;Normalized&quot; earnings per share were $.12 and $.11 for 1996 and 1995, respectively.</p>
<p>The actual earnings per share for the third quarter of 1995, which includes substantial tax credits, were $.20.</p>
</text>
